BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free Punk Rock 50th Anniversary Exhibition Opening w/ Q&A (SF)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T210000
DTSTAMP:20260831T032130Z
UID:funcheap-20260910-freepunkrock50thannivers
CATEGORIES:concert,free
DESCRIPTION:https://sf.funcheap.com/free-punk-rock-50th-anniversary-exhibi
 tion-opening-qa-sf/\nLocation: san francisco\nPrice: Free\nCategories: con
 cert\, free\nSource: funcheap/san-francisco\n\nKiel meets the Bay Area: NO
  PUNK. NO FUTURE. opens September 10 with a conversation between NO MORE a
 nd punk historian Jack Boulware. Fifty years after punk declared itself ag
 ainst everything and everyone\, the Goethe-Institut San Francisco presents
  NO PUNK. NO FUTURE. \, an exhibition exploring the connections between th
 e punk scenes of Kiel\, Germany\, and the San Francisco Bay Area. Though s
 eparated by an ocean\, both communities were driven by self-expression\, n
 onconformity\, DIY culture\, and a refusal to follow the rules. Through ph
 otography\, archival materials\, music\, and personal stories\, the exhibi
 tion traces the people\, images\, and networks that connected punk communi
 ties across the Atlantic while highlighting what made each scene unique. O
 pening Conversation Join us for a special conversation featuring: Andy A. 
 Schwarz and Tina Sanudakura of the seminal Kiel post-punk band NO MORE Jac
 k Boulware \, San Francisco writer and punk historian\, and author of Gimm
 e Something Better: The Profound\, Progressive\, and Occasionally Pointles
 s History of Bay Area Punk from Dead Kennedys to Green Day About the Exhib
 ition NO PUNK. NO FUTURE. takes its starting point from Kein Kiel \, a pro
 ject dev
LOCATION:san francisco
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/free-punk-rock-50th-anniversary-exhibition-ope
 ning-qa-sf/
END:VEVENT
